# SCAI Lucky Loop — Project Documentation

This document explains what the game actually is, how a player experiences it end to end, how the admin panel works, and how the two sides of the codebase (frontend/backend) fit together. It reflects the current, verified state of the code as of this audit — every flow described here was traced from the live source files, not from the original spec.

---

## 1. Game scenario — what SCAI Lucky Loop actually is

SCAI Lucky Loop is a **free-to-play daily lottery** with a **weekly jackpot**, playable either as a **Telegram Mini App** or directly on the **web** (no Telegram account required). Players never spend real money to play the core game — they earn a virtual currency called **coins** through daily activity and referrals, and spend coins on lottery tickets. Coins can later be converted into a real on-chain token (**LLT**, SCAI Lucky Loop Token) once a player has been active enough to qualify for withdrawal.

Think of it in three layers:

1. **Earn coins** — daily free spin, inviting friends, or (optionally) buying coins directly with SCAI or a card.
2. **Play the loop** — spend coins on numbered tickets in a daily lottery and a running weekly jackpot.
3. **Cash out** — once a player has enough coins and enough referrals, they can withdraw real LLT tokens to their own wallet.

The "loop" in the name is literal: daily draw → daily draw → daily draw, with a jackpot accumulating in the background every 7 days, endlessly repeating.

