## 3. Frontend — full player journey

The React app is served both inside Telegram (as a Mini App) and as a normal website, from the same codebase.

| Step | Screen | What happens |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Login** (`/login`) | Shows live game stats (current jackpot, player count, countdown to next draw) pulled from `/api/public/stats`, pulled from the public root as well when unauthenticated. Three sign-in paths, auto-detected: <br>• **Inside Telegram Mini App** → signs in automatically using Telegram's `initData`, no button press needed. <br>• **Plain browser, Telegram widget configured** → shows Telegram's official Login Widget. <br>• **Any browser** → "Connect wallet" (Reown AppKit) → signs a free, gas-less message to prove wallet ownership, no Telegram needed at all. A referral code in the URL (`?ref=CODE`) or Telegram's `start_param` is captured and survives page reloads via `sessionStorage`. |
| 2 | **Home** (`/home`) | Shows current coin balance (polls every 5s), a "Claim Daily Reward" spin button, and a grid linking to every other screen (Tickets, Results, Withdraw, Leaderboard, Jackpot, Profile, and Admin if the account is recognized as an admin). |
| 3 | **Tickets** (`/tickets`) | A 5×10 grid of slots 0–49 for today's draw. Sold slots are greyed out, the player's own tickets are highlighted green, everything else is purchasable (disabled entirely if balance < 10 coins). Buying a slot calls `POST /api/buy-ticket` and refreshes the grid. |
| 4 | **Draws** (`/draws`) | Shows the last 7 days of draw results — status (open/closed/drawn), winner, and a "Verify Draw" button that calls the public fairness-check endpoint. |
| 5 | **Jackpot** (`/jackpot`) | Current pool size, the week's date range and status, and a history of past weekly jackpots and their winners. |
| 6 | **Leaderboard** (`/leaderboard`) | Top players ranked by coin balance, plus the logged-in player's own rank even if they're outside the visible top list. |
| 7 | **Withdraw** (`/withdraw`) | Connect wallet → optionally buy more coins with SCAI right there → see eligibility (coins and referrals, live from the backend, never hardcoded) → submit a withdrawal request → see the resulting LLT transaction hash and a link to the block explorer. |
| 8 | **Profile** (`/profile`) | Username, coin balance, referral count, member-since date, and two separate shareable referral links — one Telegram deep link, one plain website link — since a friend needs a different link depending on whether they'll play in Telegram or in a browser. |
| 9 | **Info pages** (`/about`, `/how-it-works`, `/rules`, `/faq`, `/contact`) | Static, public, no login required — the shared marketing/informational shell (`PageShell` + `Navbar`) used across all of them. |

Every screen that needs the player's identity is wrapped in a `ProtectedRoute` that redirects to `/login` if there's no auth token; the backend independently re-verifies that token (and re-checks ban status) on every request regardless of what the frontend thinks.

